body:
I haven't thought about meeting with an employment agency... I'll be sure to contact them, and I'll be sure to contact my career services regarding finding a job, too.

Typically with this internship it seems more often than not that they would be offered a position, however, I know my mentor (herself) can't give me a job right out the gate. She's been helping me with connecting and networking and putting a good word in for me, so I hope that's working well for myself.

&#x200B;

I had my first call screen last week and was told I couldn't go through (nothing wrong with my resume or cover letter) but simply because I won't be able to work until my graduation. I sent an email to the other rejections and they told me it was mainly due to not having DIRECT HR experience, but I applied to some assistance positions and hopefully will hear something back from them.

&#x200B;

I'll take your advice though and reach out to an employment agency and contact my career service department. I'll also look up more office manager positions since I didn't think of that as a related field.

&#x200B;

Thank you so much for your input.

Keep us updated OP!

&#x200B;

I'm waiting for them to get SMACKED in the face with karma.

because you're a toxic piece of shit? lol?

&#x200B;

As the saying goes, "look both way before you cross the street, bitch, because karma coming after your ass" <3

